(53, 16, 'What is a semi-micro balance?', 'A semi-micro balance is a high-resolution laboratory balance designed for small sample quantities, commonly offering readability as fine as 0.01 mg depending on the model.', 1, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(54, 16, 'When should I use a semi-micro balance?', 'It is suitable when an analytical balance does not provide sufficient resolution but a full microbalance is not necessary. Typical applications include formulation, sample preparation, pharmaceutical testing and research.', 2, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(55, 16, 'What is a dual-range semi-micro balance?', 'A dual-range balance provides two weighing ranges. The lower range offers finer readability, while the higher range provides increased capacity with a different readability.', 3, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(56, 16, 'Why is a draft shield required?', 'At very fine readability, even small air currents can disturb the weighing result. A draft shield protects the weighing pan and improves measurement stability.', 4, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(57, 16, 'Can semi-micro balances transfer data to a computer or printer?', 'Selected models may provide communication interfaces such as RS232 or USB for data transfer, printing and connection to compatible software.', 5, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
