(78, 34, 'What is an analytical balance?', 'An analytical balance is a precision laboratory instrument commonly offering 0.1 mg readability. It is used when accurate and repeatable measurement of small quantities is required.', 1, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(79, 34, 'What applications can be performed on an analytical balance?', 'Available functions depend on the model and may include:\n• Basic weighing\n• Percentage weighing\n• Piece counting\n• Check weighing\n• Formulation and totalization\n• Density determination\n• Statistics\n• Dynamic or animal weighing', 2, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(80, 34, 'Why should the balance be levelled?', 'Correct levelling ensures that the weighing mechanism operates in its intended position. An incorrectly levelled balance may produce inaccurate or inconsistent results.', 3, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(81, 34, 'What is internal calibration?', 'Internal calibration uses a built-in reference weight to adjust the balance. On supported models, motorized internal calibration simplifies routine accuracy checks and can compensate for temperature or time-related changes.', 4, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(82, 34, 'What is the minimum sample weight?', 'Minimum sample weight is the smallest quantity that can be weighed while meeting a specified measurement uncertainty or regulatory requirement. It is different from the readability displayed by the balance.', 5, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(83, 34, 'How should an analytical balance be cleaned?', 'Remove loose powder with a soft brush and clean accessible surfaces with an appropriate lint-free cloth. Do not allow liquid or material to enter the weighing mechanism. Follow the product manual for removable draft-shield components.', 6, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(84, 35, 'What is an analytical balance?', 'An analytical balance is a precision laboratory instrument commonly offering 0.1 mg readability. It is used when accurate and repeatable measurement of small quantities is required.', 1, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
