(132, 58, 'Can a precision balance be used for piece counting?', 'Yes. Models offering piece-counting functionality calculate the number of components based on an established average piece weight.', 5, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(133, 139, 'What is a moisture analyzer?', 'A moisture analyzer combines a precision weighing system with a heating system. It determines moisture content by measuring the sample\'s weight loss during controlled drying.', 1, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(134, 139, 'What materials can be tested?', 'Moisture analyzers are used for food products, pharmaceuticals, chemicals, cosmetics, polymers, cement, agricultural materials and other products where moisture influences quality.', 2, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(135, 139, 'How much sample should be used?', 'Sample Size:\n2 g\n5 g\n10 g\nThe required sample quantity depends on the material type and measurement method. The sample should normally be spread in a thin, even layer to ensure uniform drying and accurate results.', 3, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(136, 139, 'Why do moisture results vary?', 'Variation may result from inconsistent sample size, uneven spreading, incorrect drying temperature, unsuitable shut-off criteria, contamination or differences in sample preparation.', 4, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(137, 139, 'How do I select the correct drying temperature?', 'Begin with an established reference method or compare different temperature settings against a recognized laboratory method. The temperature should remove moisture without decomposing or burning the sample.', 5, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(138, 139, 'Does a moisture analyzer require calibration?', 'Both the weighing system and heating system should be checked periodically. Weight calibration verifies weighing performance, while temperature calibration verifies the heating system.', 6, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(139, 139, 'What are the advantages of halogen heating?', 'The most important performance factor is precise and fast temperature regulation, which is best delivered by halogen lamps because of their low mass and therefore fast reaction time. This ensures repeatable results starting from the first measurement (some other heating sources either deliver different results in the first measurement or require a warm up measurement, which wastes time and resources). Furthermore, an even heat distribution on the sample surface is essential for repeatable and reliable results. We advise you to ask us or another manufacturer for a demonstration in order to experience the performance in real-life.', 7, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(140, 139, 'How can a moisture analyzer support in method development?', 'The Method Wizard is a feature of HC103, HS153, and HX204 that offers assistance in developing a suitable moisture method for specific samples. Based on the characteristics of your sample as well as a test of the drying temperature and switch-off criterion, the Method Wizard can formulate a suitable method for your sample. The Method Wizard guides you through the development of your moisture method in three simple steps:\nQuestionnaire: proposal of method parameters based on sample characteristics.\nTemperature assistant: determination of drying temperature.\nTest measurement: verification of temperature and selection of appropriate switch-off criterion.\nAfter each step of the Method Wizard, you can decide whether to accept the current method settings or to complete another step of the wizard. For steps 2 and 3, a reference moisture content value is needed.', 8, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
