(165, 442, 'What is an electronic densimeter?', 'An electronic densimeter determines the density or specific gravity of solids or liquids using measured mass values and an established calculation method as per archimedes base principal.', 1, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(166, 442, 'What is the difference between density and specific gravity?', 'Density is mass per unit volume. Specific gravity compares the density of a material with the density of a reference substance, usually water for solids and liquids.', 2, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(167, 442, 'What samples can be tested?', 'Depending on the model and accessories, densimeters may be used for metals, jewellery, gemstones, plastics, rubber, liquids and other solid materials.', 3, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(168, 442, 'Can a densimeter confirm whether jewellery is pure gold?', 'Density testing can support material evaluation, but it may not identify every alloy or plated item conclusively with any stones or diamonds. Mixed with metals which has very close density to gold & Pt. XRF analysis is more suitable when elemental composition is required. But at the same time Fake gold detection is more precise in density base  Karat analyzer.', 4, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(169, 442, 'Why must air bubbles be removed during density testing?', 'Air bubbles change the apparent displacement of the sample and can produce an incorrect density result.', 5, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(170, 443, 'What is an electronic densimeter?', 'An electronic densimeter determines the density or specific gravity of solids or liquids using measured mass values and an established calculation method as per archimedes base principal.', 1, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
