(207, 146, 'What is the difference between calibration and routine testing?', 'Calibration establishes the relationship between the displayed value and a known reference. Routine testing checks whether the balance continues to perform within defined limits between calibrations.', 3, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(208, 146, 'How should test weights be handled?', 'Use suitable tweezers, forks, gloves or weight handles. Avoid touching precision weights with bare hands because moisture, oil and dirt can alter their mass.', 4, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(209, 146, 'How should test weights be stored?', 'Store them in their original protective case in a clean, dry and temperature-stable environment.\nJEWELLERY AND PRECIOUS-METAL SOLUTIONS\nWeighing and non-destructive elemental analysis for jewellery, gold and alloy applications.', 5, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(210, 147, 'What are calibration test weights?', 'Calibration test weights are precisely manufactured mass standards used to calibrate, adjust or routinely check weighing instruments, pharma, testing lab, food and many research and testing lab who are National accrediated Board Laboratory', 1, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
