(214, 147, 'How should test weights be stored?', 'Store them in their original protective case in a clean, dry and temperature-stable environment.\nJEWELLERY AND PRECIOUS-METAL SOLUTIONS\nWeighing and non-destructive elemental analysis for jewellery, gold and alloy applications.', 5, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(215, 17, 'What is a jewellery balance?', 'A jewellery balance is designed for weighing gold, silver, diamonds, gemstones and other valuable materials with suitable capacity, readability and jewellery weighing units such as dwt, gm, ct, mg , mct, etc.', 1, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(216, 17, 'What is the difference between a gold balance and a carat balance?', 'Gold balances commonly display weight in grams and other jewellery units. Carat balances are optimized for diamonds and gemstones and generally provide finer readability at a lower capacity.', 2, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(217, 17, 'Which unit is used for weighing diamonds?', 'Diamonds and gemstones are commonly weighed in carats. One metric carat equals 200 milligrams.', 3, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(218, 17, 'Why is legal-metrology approval important?', 'When a balance is used for commercial transactions, applicable local legal-metrology requirements may need to be followed. Requirements vary by country and application.', 4, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(219, 17, 'How can jewellery weighing accuracy be maintained?', 'Keep the balance level, use it on a stable surface, avoid air movement, calibrate it regularly and ensure the weighing pan is clean before each measurement.', 5, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
