(240, 229, 'What is an XRF gold-testing machine?', 'An XRF gold-testing machine uses X-ray fluorescence to identify elements present in jewellery and precious-metal samples. The measurement is generally non-destructive and does not require cutting the sample.', 1, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(241, 229, 'Can XRF determine gold purity?', 'XRF can measure elemental composition at the tested surface and calculate gold concentration or karat value using an appropriate calibration method.', 2, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(242, 229, 'Does XRF damage jewellery?', 'Standard XRF testing is non-destructive. The sample remains physically intact during analysis.', 3, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(243, 229, 'Can XRF detect gold plating?', 'XRF analyses the region and effective depth reached by the X-rays. Thick coatings, unusual plating or layered materials may require additional investigation or specialized coating analysis.', 4, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(244, 229, 'Why can results vary at different positions?', 'Jewellery may contain solder joints, coatings, mixed alloys, stones, curved surfaces or non-uniform regions. Testing multiple representative locations improves confidence.', 5, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(245, 229, 'Does sample shape affect the result?', 'Yes. Small, curved, uneven or irregularly positioned samples can affect measurement geometry. The test area should be positioned correctly and consistently.', 6, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(246, 229, 'Is sample preparation required?', 'Most jewellery can be tested directly after cleaning the measurement area. Dirt, polishing compound, oil or surface contamination should be removed.', 7, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(247, 229, 'Is an XRF machine safe to operate?', 'XRF instruments must be used according to the manufacturer\'s instructions and applicable radiation-safety requirements. Enclosed systems use protective housing and safety features to control access during measurement.', 8, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
