(280, 239, 'What is a handheld XRF analyzer?', 'A handheld XRF analyzer is a portable instrument used for rapid, non-destructive elemental analysis at the sample location.', 1, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(281, 239, 'What materials can handheld XRF test?', 'Applications may include metals, alloys, precious metals, scrap, mining samples, components, coatings and positive material identification, depending on the instrument and calibration.', 2, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(282, 239, 'What is PMI?', 'Positive Material Identification is the verification of alloy or material composition to confirm that the correct material is being used.', 3, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(283, 239, 'Can handheld XRF detect every element?', 'The detectable element range depends on the detector, X-ray tube, calibration, measurement mode, sample and environmental conditions.', 4, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(284, 239, 'Does measurement time affect accuracy?', 'Longer measurement times can improve counting statistics and precision, particularly for elements present at low concentrations. The required time depends on the application.\nLASER SOLUTIONS\nMarking, welding and cutting systems for jewellery, industrial and precision manufacturing applications.', 5, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
