(385, 324, 'What is the difference between a bench scale and a platform scale?', 'Bench scales are generally used for smaller products on a workbench or stand. Platform scales provide larger weighing surfaces and higher capacities for cartons, containers and industrial materials.', 1, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(386, 324, 'How do I select the right capacity?', 'The scale capacity should be higher than the maximum expected load, including containers, fixtures and possible overload. Readability should also be suitable for the required process tolerance.', 2, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(387, 324, 'What is an IP rating?', 'An IP rating indicates the level of protection provided by the equipment enclosure against solid particles and water. The required rating depends on the operating environment.', 3, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(388, 324, 'Can an industrial scale connect to software?', 'Depending on the model and indicator, data may be transmitted through interfaces such as RS232, USB, Ethernet or other industrial communication options.', 4, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(389, 324, 'What is check weighing?', 'Check weighing compares the measured weight with defined lower and upper limits and indicates whether the product is underweight, acceptable or overweight.', 5, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(390, 325, 'What is the difference between a bench scale and a platform scale?', 'Bench scales are generally used for smaller products on a workbench or stand. Platform scales provide larger weighing surfaces and higher capacities for cartons, containers and industrial materials.', 1, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
