(410, 360, 'What is a load cell?', 'A load cell is a sensor that converts applied force or weight into an electrical signal.', 1, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(411, 360, 'What is a weighing indicator?', 'A weighing indicator receives the load-cell signal, processes it and displays the measured weight. It may also provide printing, communication, set-point or process-control functions.', 2, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(412, 360, 'How many load cells are required for a platform?', 'The number depends on the platform design, capacity, size and load distribution. Small platforms may use one load cell, while larger floor scales and tanks commonly use multiple load cells.', 3, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(413, 360, 'Why does a scale reading drift?', 'Drift may result from temperature variation, unstable mounting, damaged cables, moisture, electrical interference, mechanical binding or an overloaded load cell.', 4, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(414, 360, 'Can load cells be used for tank weighing?', 'Yes. Tank and hopper weighing systems use load cells with appropriate mounting assemblies, junction boxes and indicators.\nLaboratory and Analytical Instruments', 5, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(415, 361, 'What is a load cell?', 'A load cell is a sensor that converts applied force or weight into an electrical signal.', 1, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(416, 361, 'What is a weighing indicator?', 'A weighing indicator receives the load-cell signal, processes it and displays the measured weight. It may also provide printing, communication, set-point or process-control functions.', 2, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(417, 361, 'How many load cells are required for a platform?', 'The number depends on the platform design, capacity, size and load distribution. Small platforms may use one load cell, while larger floor scales and tanks commonly use multiple load cells.', 3, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(418, 361, 'Why does a scale reading drift?', 'Drift may result from temperature variation, unstable mounting, damaged cables, moisture, electrical interference, mechanical binding or an overloaded load cell.', 4, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
