(435, 524, 'What is a refractometer?', 'A refractometer measures the refractive index of a sample. Depending on the scale and method, the result may also be displayed as Brix or another concentration-related unit.', 1, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(436, 524, 'What does Brix mean?', 'Degrees Brix indicate the approximate mass percentage of sucrose in a water solution. In non-sucrose samples, Brix is an optical equivalent and should be interpreted using the relevant product method.', 2, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(437, 524, 'Does temperature affect the result?', 'Yes. Refractive index changes with temperature. Use temperature compensation where available or measure at the specified reference temperature.', 3, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(438, 524, 'How much sample is required?', 'The required volume depends on the instrument and prism size. The measuring surface must be covered fully and evenly without trapped air.', 4, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(439, 524, 'How should the prism be cleaned?', 'Remove the sample promptly with a soft, lint-free material and a suitable cleaning liquid. Avoid scratching the prism or using chemicals that can damage seals and optical surfaces.', 5, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(440, 524, 'Why do repeated readings differ?', 'Differences may result from temperature variation, incomplete prism coverage, bubbles, contamination, evaporation, non-homogeneous samples or insufficient cleaning between tests.', 6, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(441, 525, 'What is a refractometer?', 'A refractometer measures the refractive index of a sample. Depending on the scale and method, the result may also be displayed as Brix or another concentration-related unit.', 1, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
