(452, 526, 'Why do repeated readings differ?', 'Differences may result from temperature variation, incomplete prism coverage, bubbles, contamination, evaporation, non-homogeneous samples or insufficient cleaning between tests.', 6, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(453, 527, 'What is a polarimeter?', 'A polarimeter measures the angle through which an optically active sample rotates plane-polarized light.', 1, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(454, 527, 'What is specific rotation?', 'Specific rotation is a standardized value calculated from the observed rotation while accounting for sample concentration, tube length, wavelength and temperature.', 2, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(455, 527, 'Why are tube length and temperature important?', 'Optical rotation depends on the optical path length and temperature. Both must be controlled or recorded for comparable and traceable results.', 3, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(456, 527, 'How should the sample tube be filled?', 'Fill the tube completely, avoid bubbles in the light path, ensure the end windows are clean and secure the caps without introducing leakage or stress.', 4, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(457, 527, 'Can coloured or turbid samples be measured?', 'Strong colour, turbidity or suspended particles may reduce light transmission and affect the measurement. Sample preparation or an alternative method may be necessary.', 5, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(458, 527, 'What routine checks are recommended?', 'Perform zero checks with the appropriate blank and verify performance periodically using suitable reference materials or certified quartz control plates where applicable.', 6, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(459, 528, 'What is a polarimeter?', 'A polarimeter measures the angle through which an optically active sample rotates plane-polarized light.', 1, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
