(512, 488, 'How often should the cleaning solution be replaced?', 'Replace it when contaminated, when cleaning performance decreases or according to the process procedure. A visibly clean solution may still be chemically exhausted.', 6, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(513, 531, 'What does a milk analyzer measure?', 'Depending on the model and calibration, it may report parameters such as fat, solids-not-fat, protein, density, lactose, added water indication and temperature.', 1, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(514, 531, 'Why is sample mixing important?', 'Milk separates during standing. Gentle, thorough mixing produces a representative sample without creating excessive foam or air bubbles.', 2, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(515, 531, 'Does sample temperature affect the result?', 'Yes. Use the temperature range specified for the instrument and avoid testing samples that are too hot, too cold, partially frozen or poorly equilibrated.', 3, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(516, 531, 'Why is regular cleaning necessary?', 'Milk residues can block the flow path, support microbial growth and cause carryover or inaccurate measurements. Follow the prescribed rinse and cleaning sequence.', 4, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(517, 531, 'Can the analyzer replace reference laboratory methods?', 'It is useful for rapid routine screening and process control. Regulatory or dispute testing may still require an approved reference method.', 5, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(518, 531, 'Why might results differ between milk types?', 'Species, composition, processing and adulteration can affect the measurement. Use the correct calibration for the intended milk type and application.', 6, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(519, 535, 'What does a tablet hardness tester measure?', 'It measures the force required to break a tablet under controlled compression. The result helps assess mechanical strength and process consistency.', 1, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(520, 535, 'Is hardness the same as friability?', 'No. Hardness measures breaking force, while friability measures the tendency of tablets to chip, abrade or lose mass during handling.', 2, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26');
INSERT INTO `product_faqs` (`id`, `product_id`, `question`, `answer`, `sort_order`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(521, 535, 'Why is tablet orientation important?', 'Tablet shape, score line and orientation can change how the force is applied. Use a consistent orientation defined in the test method.', 3, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(522, 535, 'How many tablets should be tested?', 'The quantity should follow the approved procedure or applicable pharmacopoeial and quality requirements. A statistically meaningful sample is needed for batch evaluation.', 4, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(523, 535, 'What can cause variable hardness results?', 'Variation may arise from tablet thickness, compression force, formulation, moisture, orientation, misalignment, dirty jaws or insufficient calibration.', 5, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(524, 535, 'How is performance verified?', 'Check force accuracy and mechanical alignment using suitable certified standards or service tools according to the maintenance and calibration schedule.', 6, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(525, 532, 'What is a rotational viscometer?', 'A rotational viscometer measures the torque required to rotate a spindle in a sample at a selected speed and reports viscosity based on the instrument geometry.', 1, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(526, 532, 'Why are spindle and speed selection important?', 'The selected combination determines the measurement range and applied shear conditions. Use a combination that keeps torque within the recommended operating range.', 2, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(527, 532, 'Does temperature affect viscosity?', 'Yes, often significantly. Control and record sample temperature for repeatable and comparable results.', 3, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(528, 532, 'What is the difference between Newtonian and non-Newtonian liquids?', 'Newtonian liquids have viscosity that is relatively independent of shear rate. Non-Newtonian materials may change apparent viscosity with spindle speed, time or shear history.', 4, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(529, 532, 'Why must air bubbles be avoided?', 'Bubbles alter the spindle-sample interaction and can produce unstable or falsely low results.', 5, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(530, 532, 'How should the instrument be checked?', 'Verify level, spindle condition, zero status and performance using suitable certified viscosity standards at controlled temperature.', 6, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(531, 533, 'What is a rotational viscometer?', 'A rotational viscometer measures the torque required to rotate a spindle in a sample at a selected speed and reports viscosity based on the instrument geometry.', 1, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
