(567, 220, 'What is a coating thickness analyzer?', 'It measures the thickness of a coating or plating layer without cutting the part, provided that the coating-substrate combination is compatible with the selected method.', 1, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(568, 220, 'Which measurement methods are commonly used?', 'Depending on the application, instruments may use magnetic induction, eddy current, X-ray fluorescence or other techniques.', 2, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(569, 220, 'Why must the substrate and coating be identified?', 'The measurement principle and calibration depend on the electrical, magnetic and compositional properties of both layers.', 3, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(570, 220, 'Does surface shape affect the result?', 'Yes. Curvature, roughness, edge proximity, part thickness and probe position can affect readings. Use suitable calibration standards and consistent positioning.', 4, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(571, 220, 'How should the analyzer be calibrated?', 'Calibrate or verify it using an uncoated reference substrate and certified foils or standards that represent the expected measurement range and geometry.', 5, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
(572, 220, 'Why should several readings be taken?', 'Coatings may be non-uniform and individual readings can vary with local surface conditions. Multiple readings provide a more representative result.', 6, '2026-09-21 06:17:26', '2026-09-21 06:17:26'),
